:"hidden lg:col-start-1 lg:block lg:justify-self-end lg:pr-4","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white sticky top-28 w-52 rounded-2xl p-6","children":["$","$L13",null,{"sections":[{"_key":"what-is-the-best-ai-tool-for-jewelry-product-photos","title":"What is the best AI tool for jewelry product photos?"},{"_key":"what-to-know-before-you-pick","title":"What to know before you pick"},{"_key":"why-jewelry-is-the-hardest-product-category-to-shoot","title":"Why jewelry is the hardest product category to shoot"},{"_key":"what-separates-a-good-ai-jewelry-tool","title":"What separates a good AI jewelry tool"},{"_key":"the-seven-compared","title":"The seven compared"},{"_key":"1-melius","title":"1. Melius"},{"_key":"2-claid","title":"2. Claid"},{"_key":"3-pixelcut","title":"3. Pixelcut"},{"_key":"4-photta","title":"4. Photta"},{"_key":"5-flair","title":"5. Flair"},{"_key":"6-photoroom","title":"6. Photoroom"},{"_key":"7-comfyui","title":"7. ComfyUI"},{"_key":"when-ai-is-the-wrong-choice-for-a-piece","title":"When AI is the wrong choice for a piece"},{"_key":"building-a-jewelry-workflow-on-melius","title":"Building a jewelry workflow on Melius"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"Frequently asked questions"}],"className":"w-full flex-col gap-4 overflow-visible md:static","linkClassName":"t-b-3 !font-semibold text-foreground-muted leading-snug transition-colors hover:text-gray-dark-1","activeLinkClassName":"text-orange"}]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"wysiwyg bg-white w-full min-w-0 rounded-3xl p-6 md:p-10 lg:col-start-2 lg:p-12","children":[["$","h2","b4369",{"id":"what-is-the-best-ai-tool-for-jewelry-product-photos","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["What is the best AI tool for jewelry product photos?"]}],["$","p","b4371",{"children":["The best AI tool for jewelry product photos is the one that gives you back the exact piece you uploaded, prong count and all, instead of a plausible ring that resembles it. That sounds obvious and it's the single thing most of this category gets wrong: a model trained mostly on apparel meets a scattered-baguette ring, falls back on what a ring usually looks like, and hands you something that reads as jewelry but is not the item in your inventory. A shirt collar rendered a little differently is still the shirt. A ring with its prong count changed is a different product."]}],"$L14","$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25","$L26","$L27","$L28","$L29","$L2a","$L2b","$L2c","$L2d","$L2e","$L2f","$L30","$L31","$L32","$L33","$L34","$L35","$L36","$L37","$L38","$L39","$L3a","$L3b","$L3c","$L3d","$L3e","$L3f","$L40","$L41","$L42","$L43","$L44","$L45","$L46","$L47","$L48","$L49","$L4a","$L4b","$L4c","$L4d","$L4e","$L4f","$L50","$L51","$L52","$L53","$L54","$L55","$L56","$L57","$L58","$L59","$L5a","$L5b","$L5c","$L5d","$L5e","$L5f","$L60","$L61","$L62","$L63","$L64","$L65","$L66","$L67","$L68","$L69","$L6a"]}]]}]]}],"$L6b"]
