14:["$","p","b4373",{"children":["So the useful question isn't which tool makes the prettiest image. It's which tool holds geometry, metal and stone detail while it changes everything around them. On that test the category splits in two: general-purpose product photography tools that sell you a scene, and jewelry-first tools that sell you geometry preservation."]}]
15:["$","h2","b4375",{"id":"what-to-know-before-you-pick","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["What to know before you pick"]}]
16:["$","ul","b4377-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b4377",{"children":["Ask what the tool does to your piece. Background handling is the easy half: a swap around a cut-out preserves the product by construction, while a full regeneration redraws it."]}],["$","li","b4379",{"children":["On-model is where fidelity breaks first. Clasps, ear wires and asymmetrical pieces are the specific failure cases."]}],["$","li","b4381",{"children":["Scale decides conversions. Baymard Institute found 42% of test participants try to gauge a product's size from its images, and a ring photographed alone gives them nothing to judge against."]}],["$","li","b4383",{"children":["Over-retouching costs money later. If the piece looks better than the real thing, the gap comes back as a return."]}]]}]
17:["$","h2","b4385",{"id":"why-jewelry-is-the-hardest-product-category-to-shoot","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Why jewelry is the hardest product category to shoot"]}]
18:["$","p","b4387",{"children":["Understanding what a human photographer struggles with explains what the models struggle with, because they are the same four problems."]}]
19:["$","p","b4389",{"children":["Depth of field collapses at macro distances, often to under a millimeter at 1:1 magnification, which is why focus stacking is standard practice. Polished metal behaves like a mirror, so professionals cross-polarize, putting a filter on each light and another on the lens turned 90 degrees to them. Color is unstable across gold, rose gold and silver, which is why studios shoot a color reference at the top of every session and hold every lamp at the same temperature. And gemstones refract rather than simply reflect, so sparkle has to read as natural instead of blown out."]}]
1a:["$","p","b4391",{"children":["A generative model doesn't have any of that apparatus. It has priors. When those priors were built mostly on clothing, the model resolves an unfamiliar setting into a familiar one: claw-set reads as bezel-set, stone counts drift, fine chains blur, a domed band flattens. In March 2026 FormaNova, which sells a jewelry photography tool, put a single wide brushed-gold ring with scattered baguettes through five tools at default settings and reported that one simplified the band to a plain one, another reinterpreted the setting as channel-set, a third turned it into stacked bands, and a fourth returned something unrecognizable. The fifth was FormaNova's own tool, which preserved it. Read that ranking as marketing: the vendor graded its own exam, on one ring, three days before publishing. The failure taxonomy is worth more than the ranking, because it names specific things you can reproduce on your own hardest piece in an afternoon, which is the only test that settles it."]}]
1b:["$","h2","b4393",{"id":"what-separates-a-good-ai-jewelry-tool","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["What separates a good AI jewelry tool"]}]
1c:["$","p","b4395",{"children":["There are four criteria, and the first decides whether the output is usable at all."]}]
1d:["$","h3","b4397",{"children":["Whether your piece survives"]}]
1e:["$","p","b4399",{"children":["Look for a stated mechanism, not a promise of quality. Locking the product's position and angle while only the background changes is a mechanism. Masking a region and regenerating only outside it is a mechanism. Feeding the model real dimensions and materials, so it is not inferring them from one photograph, is a mechanism. \"Trained for jewelry\" is a claim."]}]
1f:["$","h3","b4401",{"children":["Whether it can put the piece on a person"]}]
20:["$","p","b4403",{"children":["On-model shots solve scale, and scale is worth real money. Baymard's testing found that 42% of participants try to gauge size from product images, and that when they cannot, they draw inaccurate conclusions, discarding relevant products and in some cases abandoning the site. That's what a hand, a neck or an ear is for: the size reference. It's also the hardest thing to generate, because the model has to get both the jewelry and the anatomy right, and the join between them."]}]
21:["$","h3","b4405",{"children":["Whether it holds a look across a catalog"]}]
22:["$","p","b4407",{"children":["One good image is a demo. A jewelry catalog is hundreds of stock keeping units (SKUs) that have to look like they belong to the same brand, shot the same way, across a marketplace listing, a product page and a paid social placement. That's a workflow question, and it's where single-image tools stop being useful."]}]
23:["$","h3","b4409",{"children":["What it costs to add a person who does not generate"]}]
24:["$","p","b4411",{"children":["Jewelry work gets reviewed, by a merchandiser, a founder or a client. Most tools in this category throttle on seats, and the caps are low: several cap at one, two, five or fifteen people. Worth checking before the tool becomes the reason approvals happen over email attachments."]}]
25:["$","h2","b4413",{"id":"the-seven-compared","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["The seven compared"]}]
26:["$","p","b4415",{"children":["Product fidelity counts the documented mechanisms a tool uses to keep your actual piece intact, out of five: real product details fed in as context, a reference wired into generation, masked regeneration, compositing your original asset, and a background step that preserves the cut-out. Catalog reuse asks whether one setup runs across hundreds of SKUs without being rebuilt. Team access is how many people can be in the work before it starts costing per head. Where a vendor publishes no seat data we say so instead of guessing."]}]
27:["$","div","b4416",{"role":"region","aria-label":"Comparison table, scroll horizontally to see all columns","tabIndex":0,"data-lenis-prevent":true,"className":"my-10 max-w-full overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-black/10 bg-white shadow-[0_1px_2px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-orange","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full min-w-[640px] border-collapse text-left","children":["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","b4417",{"className":"bg-black/[0.04]","children":[["$","td","b44170",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b4420",{"children":[["$","strong","b4419",{"children":["Tool"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b44171",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b4423",{"children":[["$","strong","b4422",{"children":["On-model jewelry"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b44172",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b4426",{"children":[["$","strong","b4425",{"children":["Product fidelity"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b44173",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b4429",{"children":[["$","strong","b4428",{"children":["Catalog reuse"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b44174",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b4432",{"children":[["$","strong","b4431",{"children":["Team access"]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b4433",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b44330",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4436",{"children":["Melius"]}]]}],["$","td","b44331",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4439",{"children":["Yes, with your own reference wired in"]}]]}],["$","td","b44332",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4442",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b44333",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4445",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b44334",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4448",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b4449",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b44490",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4452",{"children":["Claid"]}]]}],["$","td","b44491",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4455",{"children":["Creative mode only, vendor-hedged"]}]]}],["$","td","b44492",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4458",{"children":["3/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b44493",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4461",{"children":["3/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b44494",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4464",{"children":["Not disclosed"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b4465",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b44650",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4468",{"children":["Pixelcut"]}]]}],["$","td","b44651",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4471",{"children":["Yes, named Jewelry Scene format"]}]]}],["$","td","b44652",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4474",{"children":["2/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b44653",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b4477",{"children":["2/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b44654",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":"$L77"}]]}],"$L78","$L79","$L7a","$L7b"]}]}]}]
28:["$","h2","b4546",{"id":"1-melius","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["1. Melius"]}]
29:["$","p","b4548",{"children":["Melius is the Agentic OS for creative work. Tell it the shot you want, and the Melius agent Mel assembles the graph, picking a model per step. Every node it chooses stays editable, which for jewelry is the point: the reference wiring is where fidelity is won or lost, and that happens before anything is generated."]}]
2a:["$","p","b4550",{"children":["Two mechanisms do most of the work. The first is context: provide a product image, then add details like dimensions, materials, colors and product copy in a text node to improve the final outputs."]}]
2b:["$","p","b4552",{"children":["The second is compositing. Melius's Studio node is a layered editing surface with text overlays and custom font support, so a scene can be generated while the real asset sits on top as a layer and is never redrawn. Paired with Melius tools like Inpaint, which masks a region and regenerates only inside of it, and Remove Background, which outputs a transparent PNG for a marketplace listing that requires a pure white field, the workflow can change the world around a piece without asking a model to reinvent the piece."]}]
2c:["$","h3","b4554",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
2d:["$","ul","b4556-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b4556",{"children":["Real product details go in as context, so the model works from actual dimensions and materials."]}],["$","li","b4558",{"children":["Per-step model routing, with the documentation recommending different models for material and skin tone than for legible type."]}],["$","li","b4560",{"children":["Layered compositing, masked inpainting and background removal, so the piece survives while the scene around it changes."]}],["$","li","b4562",{"children":["Upscaling from 1K to 2K or 4K, so macro detail survives a zoom."]}],["$","li","b4564",{"children":["Magic Resize re-composes for each channel's aspect ratio instead of cropping the piece out of frame."]}],["$","li","b4566",{"children":["Up to 8 seats on self-serve plans for your team and reviewers, with unlimited seats on Enterprise."]}]]}]
2e:["$","h3","b4568",{"children":["The trade-off"]}]
2f:["$","p","b4570",{"children":["Melius is a general-purpose canvas, not a jewelry-trained system. A tool built only for jewelry has priors tuned to clasps and settings, and on a first pass with no reference wiring it may well read a complicated ring more accurately. The Melius answer is discipline: supply the real details, wire the reference, composite the asset. That works, and it asks more of you than pressing one button."]}]
30:["$","p","b4572",{"children":["Best for: jewelry brands running a catalog who want one workflow they can re-run per SKU, and who care more about the piece being right than about the first click being fast."]}]
31:["$","h2","b4574",{"id":"2-claid","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["2. Claid"]}]
32:["$","p","b4576",{"children":["Claid tells you where its own limits are. In this category that is worth more than it sounds. Its AI Photoshoot now runs five modes, and two of them carry the honest version of the fidelity question: Precise mode locks the jewelry in its original position and angle, keeping proportions and reflections intact while only the background changes, while Creative mode can alter perspective, lighting and angle, and is where on-model output comes from."]}]
33:["$","p","b4578",{"children":["It also publishes a specific limitation no other vendor here matches, warning that AI is not yet smart enough to understand complex jewelry, especially how different clasps or earwires work, and recommending flat lays over on-model for asymmetrical pieces."]}]
34:["$","h3","b4580",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
35:["$","ul","b4582-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b4582",{"children":["A documented fidelity mechanism, stated as a guarantee rather than a claim."]}],["$","li","b4584",{"children":["A published, specific account of which jewelry types it handles poorly."]}],["$","li","b4586",{"children":["Background removal, upscaling, video and an application programming interface (API) alongside the photoshoot tools."]}],["$","li","b4588",{"children":["A free trial of 50 credits, with AI Photoshoot at 4 credits per generation at standard quality and 10 at studio."]}]]}]
36:["$","h3","b4590",{"children":["The trade-off"]}]
37:["$","p","b4592",{"children":["The fidelity guarantee only holds in Precise mode, and Precise mode can't put a piece on a person, so the two things you most want are on opposite sides of a switch. Seat structure is not disclosed on the pricing page."]}]
38:["$","p","b4594",{"children":["Best for: catalog work where the background changes and the piece must not."]}]
39:["$","h2","b4596",{"id":"3-pixelcut","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["3. Pixelcut"]}]
3a:["$","p","b4598",{"children":["Pixelcut's jewelry claim is specific enough to check. It names a Jewelry Scene format for pieces worn on a wrist, neck or ear, and states that the shape, engraving, stone setting and clasp of the uploaded item are kept, with hallmarks and fine text staying crisp."]}]
3b:["$","p","b4600",{"children":["It also addresses the reflection problem directly, describing how polished gold, silver and faceted stones bounce light in ways that are hard to control, and claiming to render those highlights and mirror-like reflections cleanly."]}]
3c:["$","h3","b4602",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
3d:["$","ul","b4604-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b4604",{"children":["A named on-model jewelry format, built for the category."]}],["$","li","b4606",{"children":["An explicit, itemized fidelity claim covering engraving, setting and clasp."]}],["$","li","b4608",{"children":["Mobile-first, for a founder photographing stock on a phone."]}],["$","li","b4610",{"children":["Seats come included, not billed per head: 3 on Pro, 10 or more on Business."]}]]}]
3e:["$","h3","b4612",{"children":["The trade-off"]}]
3f:["$","p","b4614",{"children":["The fidelity claims are the vendor's own and carry no published mechanism or third-party test behind them, so they are worth verifying against your own hardest piece before committing a catalog. Its own FAQ also lists a shorter version of the guarantee than its body copy does, swapping the clasp for the metal, which is a small thing to be inconsistent about in the one claim you are selling on."]}]
40:["$","p","b4616",{"children":["Best for: small jewelry sellers who want on-model output from a phone without building a workflow."]}]
41:["$","h2","b4618",{"id":"4-photta","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["4. Photta"]}]
42:["$","p","b4620",{"children":["Photta is a fashion and apparel tool with a dedicated Jewelry Studio alongside its apparel, eyewear and product studios, and it's transparent about unit economics. It publishes per-action credit costs: 5 credits for a try-on, 4 for an AI model, 3 for a new pose, 1 for an upscale, 1 for a background."]}]
43:["$","p","b4622",{"children":["For a seller who wants to know what a hundred product shots will actually cost before signing up, that openness is useful and rare in this category."]}]
44:["$","h3","b4624",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
45:["$","ul","b4626-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b4626",{"children":["A studio built specifically for jewelry."]}],["$","li","b4628",{"children":["Per-action credit pricing published openly, so cost per SKU is calculable in advance."]}],["$","li","b4630",{"children":["Tiers scale by photo volume, from 30 photos a month to 1,000."]}],["$","li","b4632",{"children":["Try-on and pose generation as first-class actions."]}]]}]
46:["$","h3","b4634",{"children":["The trade-off"]}]
47:["$","p","b4636",{"children":["Seats are the throttle and the caps are explicit: one, two, five and fifteen across the four tiers, so collaboration is a pricing decision. There's no free plan, only a 20-credit trial that needs no card, and its published case-study conversion figure is self-reported on a single customer."]}]
48:["$","p","b4638",{"children":["Best for: sellers who want a category-specific studio and can work within a seat cap."]}]
49:["$","h2","b4640",{"id":"5-flair","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["5. Flair"]}]
4a:["$","p","b4642",{"children":["Flair is good at scene staging, with a drag-and-drop surface for arranging a product in a set, and it states that its models are trained to render fine jewelry detail including gemstone cuts, metal finishes and fine design detail. On-model output spans a range of skin tones, ages and styles."]}]
4b:["$","p","b4644",{"children":["It supports custom trained models, which is the route to a consistent house look across a catalog."]}]
4c:["$","h3","b4646",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
4d:["$","ul","b4648-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b4648",{"children":["An explicit fine-jewelry training claim covering gemstone cuts and metal finishes."]}],["$","li","b4650",{"children":["Custom model training for a repeatable brand look."]}],["$","li","b4652",{"children":["A usable free tier with one custom model and five images."]}],["$","li","b4654",{"children":["Low entry pricing, with a paid tier from $8 a month."]}]]}]
4e:["$","h3","b4656",{"children":["The trade-off"]}]
4f:["$","p","b4658",{"children":["Its own editing toolbar includes a Regenerate Product action, which is a fair signal that the product is regenerated rather than preserved, so this sits on the generative side of the fidelity line. A company commercial license first appears on the $26 tier, not the $8 one, which is worth knowing before publishing output."]}]
50:["$","p","b4660",{"children":["Best for: staged scene work where the setting matters more than millimeter-accurate geometry."]}]
51:["$","h2","b4662",{"id":"6-photoroom","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["6. Photoroom"]}]
52:["$","p","b4664",{"children":["Photoroom is good at the background half of the job and has deep tooling for it: background removal, AI backgrounds, AI shadows, a Product Beautifier and a Fix Product brush, plus video. For cut-out and re-staging work at volume it's a mature, fast option."]}]
53:["$","p","b4666",{"children":["It also generates worn jewelry through its AI virtual models, and its seat allowance is generous for a general-purpose tool, at up to 50 across paid tiers."]}]
54:["$","h3","b4668",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
55:["$","ul","b4670-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b4670",{"children":["Strong, well-established cut-out and background replacement."]}],["$","li","b4672",{"children":["AI shadows, the detail that usually gives a composite away."]}],["$","li","b4674",{"children":["Up to 50 seats on paid tiers, which is high for this category."]}],["$","li","b4676",{"children":["Worn-jewelry generation via AI virtual models, though Photoroom's own jewelry page describes them as scene placement, not on-body wear."]}]]}]
56:["$","h3","b4678",{"children":["The trade-off"]}]
57:["$","p","b4680",{"children":["The fidelity story is the weak part: it's a cut-out and background tool at heart, with generative virtual models layered on, and no stated mechanism for holding a setting or a stone count. Its jewelry performance figures are vendor-published with no methodology, and its two jewelry pages carry entirely different stat sets: one claims 2x sales growth, the other +23% conversion. A third asset, a survey of a thousand-plus jewelry brands, is the only one that states a method, and its cost-reduction figure of 93% does not match the 89% on the industry page."]}]
58:["$","p","b4682",{"children":["Best for: high-volume background and scene work, with worn shots available when a cut-out is not enough."]}]
59:["$","h2","b4684",{"id":"7-comfyui","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["7. ComfyUI"]}]
5a:["$","p","b4686",{"children":["ComfyUI is free, open source, and the option here where you control the fidelity mechanism yourself. Masked inpainting plus an explicit composite-back step lets you build a pipeline that changes a background and returns the product pixel-identical. The composite matters: the standard latent inpainting path decodes the whole frame, so unmasked areas shift measurably unless you paste the original back through the mask. That is the guarantee the commercial tools are approximating, and it holds only if you build it correctly."]}]
5b:["$","p","b4688",{"children":["For a technical operator with a catalog large enough to justify the setup, that control is real."]}]
5c:["$","h3","b4690",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
5d:["$","ul","b4692-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b4692",{"children":["Complete control over masking and compositing, so product preservation is something you can guarantee rather than trust."]}],["$","li","b4694",{"children":["Free and self-hosted, with no per-image billing on your own hardware."]}],["$","li","b4696",{"children":["Any model you can install locally, including ones no commercial platform offers, though ControlNet preprocessors and IPAdapter are community add-ons rather than core."]}],["$","li","b4698",{"children":["A deep ecosystem of community workflows for product photography."]}]]}]
5e:["$","h3","b4700",{"children":["The trade-off"]}]
5f:["$","p","b4702",{"children":["Nothing is provided, everything is assembled, and you become responsible for models, dependencies and a graphics processing unit (GPU). There's no on-model jewelry capability out of the box and collaboration is close to absent."]}]
60:["$","p","b4704",{"children":["Best for: technical operators who want a guarantee they built themselves, and have time to build it."]}]
61:["$","h2","b4706",{"id":"when-ai-is-the-wrong-choice-for-a-piece","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["When AI is the wrong choice for a piece"]}]
62:["$","p","b4708",{"children":["For a hero image on a high-value piece, hire a photographer. A one-carat solitaire on a landing page justifies cross-polarized lighting and focus stacking, and no current model beats that. Generated imagery pays off on the long tail: the hundredth SKU, the seasonal background, the channel resize, the variant nobody was going to book studio time for."]}]
63:["$","p","b4710",{"children":["There's also a floor no tool clears. If the input photograph is soft, badly lit or covered in fingerprints, the model has nothing accurate to preserve, and preservation is the whole argument. Clean the piece, shoot it sharp, then let the workflow handle everything that comes after."]}]
64:["$","h2","b4712",{"id":"building-a-jewelry-workflow-on-melius","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Building a jewelry workflow on Melius"]}]
65:["$","p","b4717",{"children":["Start with one sharp product photo and a text node carrying the details that matter: dimensions, metal, stone type, setting style. The agent routes each step to the right model, and the ",["$","$L7c","b4715",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b4714","href":"/blog/best-ai-tools-product-photo-variants","isNewTab":false},"children":["product variant workflow"]}]," applies the same way it does to any other product category, except that the composite step is non-negotiable for jewelry."]}]
66:["$","p","b4722",{"children":["Use Remove Background for marketplace listings that require a white field, Inpaint to change the scene without touching the piece, and Studio to layer the real asset over a generated background. Magic Resize re-composes for each channel's ratio instead of cropping, which matters when the piece is small and a crop loses it. The same ",["$","$L7c","b4720",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b4719","href":"/blog/best-ai-photo-background-editing-tools","isNewTab":false},"children":["background editing workflow"]}]," covers the background side in detail."]}]
67:["$","p","b4724",{"children":["The honest limit is the first pass on a piece with an unusual setting. A jewelry-specific tool's priors will read it more accurately without help. The Melius answer is to supply the help: real dimensions, real materials, a wired reference. That closes the gap, and it scales to the next hundred SKUs in a way that pressing one button a hundred times does not."]}]
68:["$","h2","b4726",{"id":"frequently-asked-questions","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Frequently asked questions"]}]
69:["$","div","b4727",{"className":"faq-list my-10 flex flex-col divide-y divide-black/10 border-y border-black/10","children":[["$","details","0",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["What is the best AI tool for jewelry product photography?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"The best AI tool for jewelry product photography depends on whether you need the background changed or the piece worn. For background and scene work where the item must not change, tools with an explicit position-locking mode, like Claid's Precise mode, do that job directly. For on-model shots and catalog workflows, a canvas that lets you supply real product data and composite the actual asset, like Melius, keeps fidelity under your control. Tools with a dedicated jewelry studio, such as Photta, are worth testing on your hardest piece."}]]}],["$","details","1",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Why do general AI photo tools struggle with jewelry?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"General AI photo tools struggle with jewelry because they were trained largely on apparel, and jewelry geometry is unfamiliar to those priors. Faced with a complicated setting, the model resolves it toward what a ring or a necklace usually looks like: prong counts change, claw settings read as bezel, stone placement drifts, and fine chains blur. The output looks like jewelry, it just isn't your jewelry, and that's a returns problem as much as an aesthetic one."}]]}],["$","details","2",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Can AI generate on-model jewelry photos of rings and necklaces?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Yes, AI can generate on-model jewelry photos of rings and necklaces, and it's the least reliable thing in the category. Pixelcut names a jewelry format for pieces worn on a wrist, neck or ear, Flair and Photta both generate worn shots, and Melius generates them on the canvas from your own reference. Claid publishes the specific limitation worth knowing: the models don't yet reliably understand how clasps and ear wires work, so asymmetrical pieces and complicated fastenings are where worn shots fail first."}]]}],"$L7d","$L7e","$L7f","$L80"]}]
6a:["$","p","b4732",{"children":["Give an agent your product image and the details that matter, and build one jewelry workflow you can re-run for every piece. ",["$","$L7c","b4730",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b4729","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true},"children":["Open Melius"]}],"."]}]
6b:["$","section","related",{"className":"relative w-full pb-section bg-gray-background","children":[["$","$L11",null,{"color":"gray"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative z-10 mx-auto w-full max-w-300 px-5 lg:px-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"t-h-2 mb-12 text-center text-balance text-gray-dark-1","children":"Related Articles"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto grid w-full max-w-max grid-cols-1 gap-11 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","$L81","post-agentic-image-generation-tools-compared",{"post":{"_key":"post-agentic-image-generation-tools-compared","slug":"agentic-image-generation-tools-compared","category":"comparisons","title":"Agentic image generation tools, compared","isoDate":"2026-09-08","date":"September 8, 2026","readTime":"13 Min Read","excerpt":"Seven tools compared on how much of the work the agent actually does: who plans the steps, who picks the models, and whether you can see and change the plan.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/agentic-image-generation-tools-compared/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Melius Team"}],"faq":[{"question":"What makes an image tool agentic rather than just AI-powered?","answer":"An image tool is agentic when it plans the work instead of executing your instructions one at a time. Anthropic draws the line plainly: workflows orchestrate LLMs and tools through predefined code paths, while agents dynamically direct their own processes and tool usage. In practice that means the tool decides how many steps a job needs, which models to use for each, and whether the result is good enough to stop. A prompt box with a conversational wrapper is not agentic, however it's marketed."},{"question":"Which agentic image tool lets you see what the agent did?","answer":"Melius and Flora both build the plan as a node graph you can open and edit, so every model choice and intermediate output is inspectable and re-runnable. Adobe returns native layered files you can take apart. Canva produces editable objects with their layers intact. Meta's Muse Image is the opposite case: its reasoning happens inside the generation call and there's nothing exposed to inspect."},{"question":"Can Claude or ChatGPT generate images through a creative tool?","answer":"Yes, Claude and ChatGPT can both generate images through a creative tool, using Model Context Protocol. Krea, Higgsfield, OpenArt, Canva, Adobe, Runway and Melius all expose MCP servers, so the assistant does the planning and the creative tool supplies the models and executes. Krea, Higgsfield and OpenArt connect over OAuth against your existing account with no API key and draw on the plan you already pay for. That setup is often the closest thing to an agentic setup here, because the planner is a frontier model."},{"question":"What is MCP and why does it matter for creative work?","answer":"Model Context Protocol is an open standard for connecting AI applications to external systems, described by its maintainers as something like a USB-C port for AI applications. Anthropic created it and donated it to the Agentic AI Foundation under the Linux Foundation in December 2025, with AWS, Google, Microsoft, OpenAI, Block, Bloomberg and Cloudflare as platinum members. For creative tools it relocates the agency: the planning and retrying can happen in your assistant while the creative tool contributes models and execution."},{"question":"Do agentic image tools work on my own files?","answer":"Some agentic image tools work on your own files and some only generate from text, and it's worth checking, because that's usually the difference between useful and decorative for brand work. Melius works on uploaded assets and can scrape a product page for real dimensions and materials, Adobe operates on Creative Cloud libraries and past campaign assets, and Canva applies your brand kit across everything it makes. Muse Image sits in between: it takes an image and edits or composes from it, but it works on the file in front of it rather than on a project's assets."},{"question":"Which is better, an agent inside the app or a general-purpose agent?","answer":"An in-app agent is better when the image is the deliverable, and a general-purpose agent is better when the image supports a larger job. Iterating on an image needs the ability to change step three without redoing steps four through ten, and that is what a general agent lacks. Genspark has a canvas and editable layers, and plans across many tools well; what it doesn't keep is the graph, so the tenth revision costs as much as the first."},{"question":"Does an agent replace the creative direction?","answer":"No, an agent does not replace the creative direction, and the tools that pretend otherwise produce work nobody ships. The agent handles assembly: wiring the pipeline, choosing a model per step, running and re-running. The brief, the judgment about whether a result is right, and the decision about what to make at all remain yours. What changes is how much of your time goes into the mechanical part, which was never the creative part."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"what-are-agentic-image-generation-tools","title":"What are agentic image generation tools?"},{"_key":"what-to-know-before-you-pick","title":"What to know before you pick"},{"_key":"the-test-this-list-is-built-on","title":"The test this list is built on"},{"_key":"where-the-agency-actually-lives","title":"Where the agency actually lives"},{"_key":"the-seven-compared","title":"The seven compared"},{"_key":"1-melius","title":"1. Melius"},{"_key":"2-flora","title":"2. Flora"},{"_key":"3-adobe-firefly-ai-assistant","title":"3. Adobe Firefly AI Assistant"},{"_key":"4-canva-ai","title":"4. Canva AI"},{"_key":"5-meta-muse-image","title":"5. Meta Muse Image"},{"_key":"6-krea-over-mcp","title":"6. Krea over MCP"},{"_key":"7-genspark","title":"7. Genspark"},{"_key":"when-you-don-t-want-an-agent","title":"When you don't want an agent"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"Frequently asked questions"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4001","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4000","text":"What are agentic image generation tools?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-are-agentic-image-generation-tools"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4003","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4002","text":"An agentic image tool is one where you describe an outcome and something plans the work, picks the models, runs the steps and checks its own results, instead of you specifying each step yourself. Anthropic draws the useful line: workflows orchestrate LLMs and tools through predefined code paths, while agents dynamically direct their own processes and tool usage, keeping control over how they accomplish a task. Most products marketed as agentic image generators are workflows with a chat box in front.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4005","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4004","text":"So this comparison ranks on agency, not on image quality. That's a deliberate departure from most roundups in this category, which sort on realism, prompt fidelity and price. Those pages are answering a different question.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4007","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4006","text":"What to know before you pick","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-to-know-before-you-pick"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4009","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4008","text":"Agency lives in one of four places, and which one you want depends on where the rest of your work already happens: the app's orchestrator, the model itself, a general-purpose agent, or the assistant you already use.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4011","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4010","text":"Ask whether you can see the plan. An agent that returns a finished image and no steps has made every decision on your behalf, which is fine until it's wrong.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4013","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4012","text":"Check what a reviewer costs. Most tools here bill per seat, so the person who approves the work needs a license before they can look at it, and a small team can pay more in seats than in generation.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4015","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4014","text":"Check whether it works on your assets or only generates from text. For brand and product work this is usually the difference between useful and decorative.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4017","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4016","text":"The test this list is built on","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"the-test-this-list-is-built-on"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4019","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4018","text":"There are four questions, and they apply to every tool here. They are drawn from how Anthropic defines an agent, and a tool has to pass more than one to count.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4021","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4020","text":"Does it plan multi-step work from a single stated goal? Does it choose its own tools and models, or does it hand you a dropdown? Does it check its own output and try again if the first result is wrong? And is the plan something you can open and change?","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4023","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4022","text":"That last question is where the interesting disagreement sits. Autonomy and control are usually traded against each other, and the tools that score highest on planning often score lowest on inspectability. The ones worth using are the ones that refuse the trade.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4025","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4024","text":"Where the agency actually lives","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"where-the-agency-actually-lives"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4027","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4026","text":"Four architectures, and they behave differently enough to be four different products.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4029","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4028","text":"In the app's orchestrator","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4031","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4030","text":"The tool has its own planner that reads your brief, builds a sequence of steps, and runs them. This is the category most people mean, and it's where the work stays visible if the product is built that way. Melius, Flora, the Adobe Firefly AI Assistant and Canva all sit here.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4033","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4032","text":"In the model itself","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4035","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4034","text":"A newer and stranger case: the model plans, calls tools and self-corrects during generation, with no orchestrator above it. Meta's Muse Image is the clearest example, and Meta reports that its self-refinement behavior emerged during reinforcement learning and was never programmed. There's nothing to inspect here, because the reasoning happens inside a single generation call.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4037","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4036","text":"In a general-purpose agent","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4039","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4038","text":"A broad agent treats an image as one sub-task inside a larger job, routing across many tools. Genspark and Manus work this way. Strong when the image is part of a research or document task, weaker when the image is the deliverable and the work has to be re-run.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4041","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4040","text":"In the assistant you already use","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4046","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b4043","href":"/blog/connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4042","text":"The most under-covered option. Model Context Protocol is an open standard, created by Anthropic and donated to the Agentic AI Foundation under the Linux Foundation in December 2025, with AWS, Google, Microsoft, OpenAI, Block, Bloomberg and Cloudflare among its platinum members. When a creative tool ships an MCP server, Claude or ChatGPT does the planning and retrying, and the creative tool supplies the models. Krea, Higgsfield, OpenArt, Canva, Adobe, Runway and Melius all expose one, and we've written on ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4044","text":"connecting AI agents to a canvas over MCP","marks":["b4043"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4045","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4048","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4047","text":"The seven compared","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"the-seven-compared"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4050","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4049","text":"Capabilities taken from each vendor's own documentation. Steps visible means you can see and change what the agent decided, down to the individual model call.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"portableTable","_key":"b4051","rows":[{"_key":"b4052","cells":[{"_key":"b4053","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4055","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4054","text":"Tool","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b4056","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4058","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4057","text":"Where agency lives","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b4059","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4061","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4060","text":"Steps visible","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b4062","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4064","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4063","text":"Cross-provider models","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b4065","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4067","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4066","text":"Drive from outside","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b4068","cells":[{"_key":"b4069","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4071","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4070","text":"Melius","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4072","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4074","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4073","text":"App orchestrator, or your assistant","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4075","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4077","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4076","text":"Yes, as an editable graph","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4078","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4080","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4079","text":"Every leading model, routed per step","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4081","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4083","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4082","text":"Slack, MCP, CLI and API","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b4084","cells":[{"_key":"b4085","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4087","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4086","text":"Flora","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4088","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4090","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4089","text":"App orchestrator","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4091","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4093","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4092","text":"Yes, as an editable graph","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4094","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4096","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4095","text":"Yes, 50+ advertised, more in its docs","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4097","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4099","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4098","text":"API and MCP","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b4100","cells":[{"_key":"b4101","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4103","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4102","text":"Adobe Firefly","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4104","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4106","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4105","text":"App orchestrator","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4107","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4109","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4108","text":"Yes, native editable files","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4110","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4112","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4111","text":"Partner models, agent-selected","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4113","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4115","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4114","text":"Claude, ChatGPT and Slack","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b4116","cells":[{"_key":"b4117","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4119","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4118","text":"Canva","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4120","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4122","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4121","text":"App orchestrator","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4123","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4125","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4124","text":"Yes, editable objects","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4126","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4128","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4127","text":"Its own design model, plus third-party generators","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4129","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4131","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4130","text":"MCP and connectors","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b4132","cells":[{"_key":"b4133","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4135","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4134","text":"Meta Muse Image","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4136","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4138","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4137","text":"The model itself","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4139","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4141","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4140","text":"No","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4142","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4144","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4143","text":"No, single model","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4145","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4147","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4146","text":"Via developer platforms","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b4148","cells":[{"_key":"b4149","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4151","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4150","text":"Krea","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4152","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4154","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4153","text":"Your assistant, over MCP","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4155","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4157","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4156","text":"In the assistant's transcript","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4158","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4160","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4159","text":"Yes, wide roster","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4161","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4163","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4162","text":"MCP, no API key required","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b4164","cells":[{"_key":"b4165","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4167","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4166","text":"Genspark","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4168","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4170","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4169","text":"General-purpose agent","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4171","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4173","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4172","text":"Partly","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4174","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4176","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4175","text":"Yes, 80+ models","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b4177","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b4179","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4178","text":"Within its own app","marks":[]}]}]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4181","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4180","text":"1. Melius","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"1-melius"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4183","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4182","text":"Melius is the Agentic OS for creative work, and the first node-based canvas made for agents. You describe what you want, then Melius's agent Mel plans the work, wires it as a graph, routes each node to the model that suits that step, and runs it. The plan is not a hidden reasoning trace, it's the canvas: every prompt, model choice and intermediate output is a node you can open, change and re-run.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4185","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4184","text":"That is how Melius answers the autonomy-versus-control trade: a chat thread loses the process, and a graph keeps it. Change an early node and everything downstream can re-run, branch to compare two directions, or keep a working graph and point it at next week's inputs.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4187","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4186","text":"The agency can also live somewhere other than the app. Melius exposes its tools over MCP at mcp.melius.com, so Claude or ChatGPT can plan and drive the canvas. Slack, a command-line interface (CLI) and an application programming interface (API) all act on the same canvas. Other tools here are reachable from Claude, ChatGPT and Slack too, but the difference is the command line and the fact that all four routes land on the same canvas. Multiple people and multiple agents work on it at once, with agents claiming a region while they work so nobody collides. Throughout, the direction is yours: the agent does the wiring and the running, and the taste and the final call stay with you.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4189","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4188","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4191","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4190","text":"The agent's plan is the artifact you edit, so nothing about the decision is hidden.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4193","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4192","text":"Per-step routing across image, video and audio models from several providers.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4195","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4194","text":"Tools over MCP, plus Slack, a CLI and an API, so the planning can happen in the assistant you already use, or in your terminal.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4197","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4196","text":"Several agents and several people on one canvas at once, with a region claim required before an agent can change any node, so two agents cannot quietly overwrite each other.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4199","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4198","text":"Works on your uploaded assets, and scrapes a product page for real dimensions and materials.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4201","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4200","text":"Up to 8 seats on self-serve plans, including the free tier, and unlimited seats on Enterprise.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4203","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4202","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4205","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4204","text":"An agent is only as good as the brief, and a vague description produces a vague graph, at which point you're opening the canvas whether you wanted to or not. The Slack integration is gated to the Professional tier and above, and the entry plan caps agent skills, so the fuller agentic surface is not the cheapest thing here.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4213","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b4207","href":"/pricing","isNewTab":false},{"_type":"link","_key":"b4210","href":"/models","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4206","text":"Current pricing is on the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4208","text":"pricing page","marks":["b4207"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4209","text":", the current library of leading models is on the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4211","text":"models page","marks":["b4210"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4212","text":", and the MCP tool reference is in the docs.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4215","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4214","text":"Best for: teams who want an agent to do the assembly and still want to see and change every decision it made.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4217","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4216","text":"2. Flora","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"2-flora"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4219","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4218","text":"Flora is good at the same architectural idea and arrived at it independently. Its FAUNA agent reads the canvas, adds nodes, chooses models, connects pipelines, runs generations and organizes the output, building the workflow in real time while you watch and steer. Flora's own framing is that every step appears on the canvas as it happens, and that the models, prompts and sequence live on the canvas when the session ends. It won't spend your usage budget without asking: Assist mode, the default, confirms and prices the work first, though an Auto mode runs without pausing.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4224","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b4221","href":"/blog/flora-alternative","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4220","text":"Its homepage counts 50 or more models and its pricing page 60 or more alongside four it names, while its own docs catalogue runs past a hundred, spanning image, video, text, audio and upscaling. API and MCP access come with every paid tier. We've compared it in more detail in our ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4222","text":"Flora alternative","marks":["b4221"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4223","text":" post.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4226","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4225","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4228","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4227","text":"An agent that builds complete workflows on a visible canvas you can edit.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4230","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4229","text":"Fifty or more models across several providers, chosen by the agent per step.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4232","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4231","text":"An Assist mode, on by default, that confirms and prices the work before it spends any of your budget.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4234","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4233","text":"API and MCP on every paid tier, including the entry plan.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4236","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4235","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4238","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4237","text":"Pricing is per seat, so collaboration scales linearly with cost. The free tier is text and image only and capped at a small usage allowance, which Flora illustrates as about seventeen images, and it carries no API or MCP access, which makes the agentic surface hard to evaluate before paying.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4240","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4239","text":"Best for: solo creators and small teams who want an agent-built graph and can absorb per-seat pricing.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4242","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4241","text":"3. Adobe Firefly AI Assistant","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"3-adobe-firefly-ai-assistant"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4244","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4243","text":"The Firefly assistant orchestrates multi-step work across separate professional applications. It executes across Photoshop, Premiere, Illustrator, InDesign and Frame.io from a described outcome, with After Effects in private beta, and the outputs are native Adobe files that keep pixel-level control, so you can step in at any point to refine or redirect.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4246","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4245","text":"It doesn't stay inside Adobe either. Adobe ships connectors for Claude and ChatGPT, and an Adobe for Slack MCP app exposing more than seventy Adobe tools. Model choice is delegated by default too: Adobe's own FAQ says the assistant selects across Firefly and partner models depending on the request, unless you name one.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4248","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4247","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4250","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4249","text":"Multi-step orchestration across Photoshop, Premiere, Illustrator, InDesign and Frame.io.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4252","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4251","text":"Output lands as native, layered, editable files.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4254","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4253","text":"Connectors for Claude, ChatGPT and Slack, with more than seventy Adobe tools exposed.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4256","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4255","text":"Works on Creative Cloud libraries and prior campaign assets.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4258","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4257","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4260","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4259","text":"It's the ecosystem that constrains this, not the agent. Everything it produces lands in Adobe formats and assumes you are a Creative Cloud subscriber, the assistant is still in public beta across the apps, and the model roster is Adobe's curated partner set rather than anything you can point at yourself. The Slack route also requires a Slack Business+ or Enterprise+ plan.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4262","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4261","text":"Best for: teams already inside Creative Cloud who want work executed across apps and returned as editable files.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4264","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4263","text":"4. Canva AI","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"4-canva-ai"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4266","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4265","text":"Canva is building toward running work when you aren't there. Canva AI 2.0 schedules recurring background tasks such as a weekly batch of social assets, runs web research before it generates, and carries brand context across sessions in a Memory Library. Canva's own product page still marks it coming soon, so treat this as capability on the way.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4268","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4267","text":"Output arrives as individual editable objects and layers, and Brand Intelligence applies an organization's fonts, colors and style, including to work already made.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4270","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4269","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4272","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4271","text":"Scheduled recurring tasks, so a weekly batch runs when nobody is in the app.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4274","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4273","text":"A Memory Library that carries brand and preferences across sessions.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4276","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4275","text":"Output as editable objects with layers intact.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4278","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4277","text":"A remote MCP server connected in twenty-one clients, ChatGPT, Claude, Codex, xAI's Grok and Perplexity Computer among them.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4280","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4279","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4282","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4281","text":"Canva composes with its own Design Model and reaches out to third-party models for the generation itself, Google's Veo 3 among them, so the roster is not the limit. What you give up is the choice: which model runs a given step stays Canva's call. It's also priced per person, and the fuller AI allowance is a per-person monthly add-on on top of that.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4284","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4283","text":"Best for: marketing teams who want recurring output produced automatically inside one brand system.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4286","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4285","text":"5. Meta Muse Image","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"5-meta-muse-image"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4288","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4287","text":"Muse Image fits the definition literally, and it isn't a product with an agent attached. The model itself invokes search and coding tools to improve accuracy, self-refines its own generations, and improves by spending more compute at generation time. It will write and execute code to produce a plot or a QR code, then condition on the rendered result to improve the image.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4290","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4289","text":"Meta reports the self-refinement was not programmed but emerged during reinforcement learning, and that human-preference Elo scales roughly log-linearly with reasoning effort on its own internal ablation, with deliberate reasoning outperforming simply generating many candidates and picking one.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4292","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4291","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4294","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4293","text":"Genuine tool use and self-correction inside a single generation.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4296","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4295","text":"Web search grounding, so images can reflect current real-world facts.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4298","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4297","text":"It writes and runs code to produce plots and QR codes, then conditions on the rendered result, though Meta publishes no accuracy figures.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4300","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4299","text":"Available to developers through Meta's own API, fal and OpenRouter, with Meta also listing Runway.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4302","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4301","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4304","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4303","text":"There is nothing to inspect and nothing to steer. The reasoning happens inside the generation call, with no documented control over the number of steps or the plan, so when the result is wrong your only lever is the prompt. It's a single model, not a workflow tool. It does take image input, editing an existing image and composing across several reference images, though there's no pipeline to keep and nothing to re-run.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4306","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4305","text":"Best for: single images that need factual grounding or precise rendered detail, where you don't need to direct the process.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4308","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4307","text":"6. Krea over MCP","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"6-krea-over-mcp"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4310","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4309","text":"Krea's MCP server is a cheap, honest way to try this architecture, and it demonstrates the pattern well: the agency lives in Claude or ChatGPT, and Krea supplies the models. The assistant plans, calls the tools, looks at what came back and tries again.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4312","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4311","text":"Krea's MCP page names Flux, Hailuo, Runway, Kling, Ideogram and Nano Banana Pro among more than forty models, and it connects over OAuth, the standard sign-in handshake, against your existing account with no API key required, billing the workspace you pick as you approve it, which removes the usual objection that this needs a developer.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4314","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4313","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4316","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4315","text":"The planner is whichever assistant you already use, and it improves as that model improves.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4318","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4317","text":"No API key required, connecting over OAuth in about a minute.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4320","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4319","text":"A wide model roster reachable through a single connection.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4322","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4321","text":"Works from Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor and several other clients.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4324","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4323","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4326","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4325","text":"The record of the work is a chat transcript, so there's no persistent artifact to re-run, branch or hand to a colleague. Multi-step image work over a conversation is also slow, since each step is a round trip. Krea's free tier excludes its node canvas entirely, so the MCP route is the agentic surface on the cheaper plans.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4328","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4327","text":"Best for: people who live in an assistant and want image generation available there without adopting another interface.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4330","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4329","text":"7. Genspark","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"7-genspark"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4332","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4331","text":"Genspark is good when the image is one part of a bigger job. Its Super Agent plans tasks and routes across more than eighty models, and its Mixture-of-Agents architecture runs several expert agents in parallel, each handling what it does best, then synthesizes the output.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4334","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4333","text":"That mode is worth noting because it delegates the model decision instead of handing it back to you, which most tools claiming to be agentic won't do.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4336","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4335","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4338","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4337","text":"Genuine task planning across more than eighty models, with images as one capability among many.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4340","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4339","text":"Mixture-of-Agents runs several expert agents in parallel and synthesizes one result.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4342","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4341","text":"Image models it lists include Nano Banana Pro, GPT Image 2, Seedream V5, Flux 2 Pro, Ideogram V3 and Recraft V3.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4344","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4343","text":"A free tier with a daily credit allowance.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4346","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4345","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4348","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4347","text":"The creative surface is better equipped than the general-agent label suggests: there's a canvas, elements stay editable, it exports PSD and PPTX, and you can inpaint or outpaint and feed the result back as a reference. What's missing is the graph. Nothing records the sequence of decisions, so changing an early one means redoing by hand everything that followed it. Fine when the image serves a document or a research output, frustrating when the image is the deliverable and needs ten rounds.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4350","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4349","text":"Best for: research and document work where images are produced along the way.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4352","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4351","text":"When you don't want an agent","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"when-you-don-t-want-an-agent"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4354","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4353","text":"For one image from one clear idea, an agent is overhead. Open a strong model, prompt it, and you're finished before a planner has decided what to do. The same goes for work where you already know the exact sequence: if you can specify the steps faster than you can describe the outcome, specify them.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4359","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b4356","href":"/blog/best-ai-creative-canvases-image-generation","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4355","text":"Agents pay off on multi-step work you'd otherwise assemble by hand, and on work you'll run repeatedly. That's also where the visible-plan question stops being philosophical. Delegating the assembly of a twelve-step pipeline is worth a great deal; delegating it to something that won't show you what it built is worth considerably less, because the first time the output is subtly wrong you have no way in. The tools that keep the plan on the canvas are betting you'll eventually want to look. On anything you'll re-run, that bet pays, which is the same case for a ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4357","text":"node-based creative canvas","marks":["b4356"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4358","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4361","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4360","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b4362","items":"$6b:props:children:1:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:post:faq"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b4367","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b4364","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b4363","text":"Describe the outcome and let an agent plan the steps, pick a model for each and wire the graph, from the canvas or from Slack, then open any node to change what it decided. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4365","text":"Open Melius","marks":["b4364"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b4366","text":".","marks":[]}]}]}}],"$L82","$L83"]}]]}]]}]
